My recommendation: Start with a smaller version
I would avoid incorporating AI or machine learning immediately.
Start by building a program that:
Accepts any reasonably structured CSV or Excel file.
Identifies the different data types.
Checks for data quality issues.
Automatically calculates relevant statistics.
Identifies trends, correlations, and anomalies.
Generates a written report with charts.
Once that works, introduce AI to help interpret the findings and generate more sophisticated explanations.
One question that will determine how I'd approach this project:
What is your ultimate vision for the program?
A. General-purpose data analyst: Upload virtually any dataset, and it automatically analyzes the information and generates insights.
B. Business intelligence tool: Primarily analyzes business data such as sales, revenue, expenses, operations, and customers.
C. AI-powered data analyst: Upload a dataset and interact with it conversationally, asking questions like "What is causing sales to decrease?" or "What are the biggest opportunities in this data?"
D. Automated research assistant: Takes datasets and produces comprehensive, professional reports with statistical findings, visualizations, and written conclusions.
These are quite different engineering projects, and choosing the right direction early will save you a lot of development time.
